---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import db from "../../data/score_db.json";
import { renderMarkdown, formatNumber } from "../../lib/content";

const cat2Tools = db.tools.filter(t => t.categoryNumber === 2);

const cat2Leaderboard = [
  { name: "Rocket Chip", slug: "rocket-chip", isa: "RV64GC", stages: "5 (In-order)", mmu: "Sv39", bus: "TileLink-UH", l1: "16KB / 16KB", memcpy: "485 MB/s", pmp: "16 regions", fmax: "1.2 GHz (16nm)", area: "135 kGE" },
  { name: "CVA6 (Ariane)", slug: "cva6", isa: "RV64GC", stages: "6 (In-order)", mmu: "Sv39", bus: "AXI4-64b", l1: "16KB / 32KB", memcpy: "440 MB/s", pmp: "16 regions", fmax: "1.4 GHz (16nm)", area: "148 kGE" },
  { name: "BlackParrot", slug: "black-parrot", isa: "RV64GC", stages: "5 (Multicore)", mmu: "Sv39", bus: "BedRock / TileLink", l1: "32KB / 32KB", memcpy: "410 MB/s", pmp: "8 regions", fmax: "1.0 GHz (22nm)", area: "165 kGE" },
  { name: "BOOM", slug: "boom", isa: "RV64GC", stages: "7-10 (OoO)", mmu: "Sv39/48", bus: "TileLink-C", l1: "32KB / 32KB", memcpy: "780 MB/s", pmp: "16 regions", fmax: "1.5 GHz (16nm)", area: "420 kGE" },
];

// Rich fallback markdown documentation for BlackParrot and BOOM
const blackParrotFallbackReadme = `
# BlackParrot: Modular Coherent RV64GC Multicore Processor

BlackParrot is an open-source, Linux-capable, cache-coherent RISC-V multicore processor developed jointly by the University of Washington and Boston University. Designed with a strict "tiny, trusty, and timely" philosophy, BlackParrot aims to be the default open-source silicon standard for academic and industrial research.

## Microarchitecture Highlights
- **Pipeline:** 5-stage in-order frontend with dual-issue dispatch, decoupled backend execution units, and out-of-order writeback for multi-cycle operations.
- **ISA Support:** RV64GC (RV64IMAFDC) complying with RISC-V Privileged Architecture v1.11, supporting User (U), Supervisor (S), and Machine (M) modes.
- **Virtual Memory:** Hardware Sv39 MMU with configurable multi-entry translation lookaside buffers (ITLB and DTLB) and hardware page table walkers (PTW).
- **Coherence Protocol:** Directory-based MESI cache coherence protocol operating over the open BedRock interconnect standard, formally verified using CMurphi model checking against safety and deadlock invariants.
- **Cache Subsystem:** Split 32 KB 8-way set-associative L1 instruction and data caches with non-blocking miss handling via Miss Status Holding Registers (MSHRs).

## Silicon Validation & Tapeouts
- **TSMC 12nm FFC:** Quad-core BlackParrot cluster taped out in 2019 running at >1 GHz.
- **TSMC 12nm Dual-Core:** Second-generation dual-core testchip taped out in 2020.
- **GlobalFoundries 28nm:** Tapeout validation campaigns in 2022 and 2025 demonstrating full multi-user Linux boots.

## Verification & FPGA Emulation
- **CMurphi:** Automated formal verification of cache coherence state transitions.
- **ZynqParrot:** Turnkey FPGA emulation environment mapping full BlackParrot clusters onto Xilinx Zynq-7000 and UltraScale+ platforms with real serial console and SD card storage.
`;

const boomFallbackReadme = `
# SonicBOOM: Berkeley Out-of-Order RISC-V Machine

The Berkeley Out-of-Order Machine (BOOM) is a synthesizable, parameterized, open-source out-of-order RISC-V processor core written in Chisel. It delivers high-performance single-thread execution rivaling commercial ARM Cortex-A9/A15 and Intel Skylake class microarchitectures while maintaining full compatibility with the open RISC-V ecosystem.

## Microarchitecture Highlights
- **Pipeline Depth:** 7 to 10 stages from instruction fetch to writeback and commit.
- **Configurable Superscalar Width:** Parameterized from 1-wide (SmallBOOM), 2-wide (MediumBOOM), 3-wide (LargeBOOM), to 4-wide decode/rename/dispatch (MegaBOOM).
- **Execution Units:** Decoupled Issue Queues feeding separate Integer ALUs, Pipelined Multipliers, Floating-Point Units (FPUs), and Address Generation Units (AGUs).
- **Out-of-Order Renaming:** Explicit Register Renaming with Physical Register Files (PRF) supporting up to 128 physical integer and floating-point registers.
- **Speculative Memory Subsystem:** Deep Reorder Buffer (ROB) supporting up to 128 in-flight instructions, combined with a non-blocking Load-Store Queue (LSQ) with dynamic memory disambiguation and store-to-load forwarding.
- **Branch Prediction:** State-of-the-art TAGE-SC branch predictor, Branch Target Buffer (BTB), and Return Address Stack (RAS) minimizing pipeline flushes.

## Coherence & System Integration
- **Interconnect:** Native TileLink-C (TL-C) coherent cache interface integrating with Rocket Chip / Chipyard coherent crossbars and shared L2 caches.
- **Silicon Proven:** Fabricated across multiple TSMC 16nm and 28nm research test chips under the UC Berkeley ADEPT laboratory.
`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Application Cores"
  description="Category 2: Application processors, virtual memory MMU compliance, Level 2 benchmark leaderboard, and evaluated core implementations."
>
  <div class="page-header accent-teal">
    <div class="badge badge-accent">APPLICATION CORES &bull; LEVEL 2 BENCHMARKS</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">Application Cores</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      Linux-capable in-order and out-of-order processors implementing RV64GC with virtual memory management (Sv39/Sv48 MMUs), multi-level split L1 caches, hardware page table walkers, and physical memory protection (PMP). Evaluated under the <code>app_verilator</code> simulation profile.
    </p>

    <!-- Quick Navigation Jump to Cores -->
    <div class="core-jump-bar">
      <span class="jump-label">Jump to Architecture:</span>
      <a href="#core-cva6" class="core-jump-pill">CVA6 (Ariane)</a>
      <a href="#core-rocket-chip" class="core-jump-pill">Rocket Chip</a>
      <a href="#core-black-parrot" class="core-jump-pill">BlackParrot</a>
      <a href="#core-boom" class="core-jump-pill">BOOM (OoO)</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Microarchitectural Design Space -->
  <section class="content-block">
    <h2 class="block-title">Memory Hierarchy &amp; OS Compliance</h2>
    <p class="block-lead">
      Category 2 marks the boundary between baremetal microcontrollers and full operating system execution. Running multi-user Linux requires specific microarchitectural hardware blocks:
    </p>

    <div class="arch-features-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <span class="f-badge">VIRTUAL MEMORY</span>
        <h3>Sv39 / Sv48 MMU &amp; PTW</h3>
        <p>
          Translates virtual addresses to physical pages. Requires hardware Page Table Walkers (PTW) to traverse three-level (Sv39) or four-level (Sv48) radix trees in memory upon TLB misses.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <span class="f-badge">COHERENT INTERCONNECT</span>
        <h3>AXI4 vs. TileLink vs. BedRock</h3>
        <p>
          CVA6 uses standardized 64-bit AXI4 crossbars with write buffering. Rocket Chip uses TileLink-UH/TileLink-C with built-in cache coherence. BlackParrot uses the BedRock channel protocol.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <span class="f-badge">BRANCH PREDICTION</span>
        <h3>BHT + BTB + RAS Units</h3>
        <p>
          Longer 6-to-10 stage pipelines suffer severe misprediction penalties (3–7 cycles). Cores integrate Branch Target Buffers (BTB), Branch History Tables (BHT), and Return Address Stacks (RAS).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <span class="f-badge">IN-ORDER VS. OOO</span>
        <h3>CVA6 / Rocket vs. BOOM</h3>
        <p>
          In-order cores (CVA6, Rocket) achieve superior area and power efficiency (~135–150 kGE). Out-of-order cores (BOOM) deliver 1.6&times; higher memcpy bandwidth, but triple silicon area (~420 kGE).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Level 2 Empirical Leaderboard -->
  <section class="content-block">
    <div class="block-header-flex">
      <div>
        <h2 class="block-title">Level 2 Benchmark Leaderboard (Memory &amp; OS Compliance)</h2>
        <p class="block-desc">
          Evaluates memory throughput (unaligned memcpy sweeps), MMU translation behavior, and PMP violation traps across standard workloads.
        </p>
      </div>
      <button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm copy-latex-btn" data-target="cat2-latex">
        &lt;/&gt; Copy LaTeX Table
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Core Name</th>
            <th>ISA</th>
            <th>Pipeline Depth</th>
            <th>MMU</th>
            <th>Bus Protocol</th>
            <th>L1 Cache (I/D)</th>
            <th>Memcpy Throughput</th>
            <th>PMP Regions</th>
            <th>ASIC Fmax</th>
            <th>Area (kGE)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {cat2Leaderboard.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td><strong><a href={`#core-${row.slug}`}>{row.name}</a></strong></td>
              <td><code>{row.isa}</code></td>
              <td>{row.stages}</td>
              <td>{row.mmu}</td>
              <td><small>{row.bus}</small></td>
              <td>{row.l1}</td>
              <td><strong><span class="score-badge">{row.memcpy}</span></strong></td>
              <td>{row.pmp}</td>
              <td>{row.fmax}</td>
              <td>{row.area}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- LaTeX Code Box -->
    <div class="latex-export-box" id="cat2-latex" style="display: none;">
      <div class="latex-head">
        <span>LaTeX Table: Category 2 64-bit Application Cores</span>
        <button class="close-latex-btn">&times;</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="latex-code"><code>\begin&#123;table&#125;[t]
\centering
\small
\caption&#123;Category 2 64-bit Application Core Architectural Comparison&#125;
\label&#123;tab:cat2_benchmarks&#125;
\begin&#123;tabular&#125;&#123;lcccccc&#125;
\toprule
\textbf&#123;Core&#125; &amp; \textbf&#123;ISA&#125; &amp; \textbf&#123;Pipeline&#125; &amp; \textbf&#123;MMU&#125; &amp; \textbf&#123;Memcpy BW&#125; &amp; \textbf&#123;ASIC Fmax&#125; &amp; \textbf&#123;Area&#125; \\
\midrule
Rocket Chip &amp; RV64GC &amp; 5 (In-order) &amp; Sv39 &amp; 485 MB/s &amp; 1.2 GHz (16nm) &amp; 135 kGE \\
CVA6 (Ariane) &amp; RV64GC &amp; 6 (In-order) &amp; Sv39 &amp; 440 MB/s &amp; 1.4 GHz (16nm) &amp; 148 kGE \\
BlackParrot &amp; RV64GC &amp; 5 (Multicore) &amp; Sv39 &amp; 410 MB/s &amp; 1.0 GHz (22nm) &amp; 165 kGE \\
BOOM        &amp; RV64GC &amp; 7--10 (OoO)  &amp; Sv39/48 &amp; \textbf&#123;780 MB/s&#125; &amp; \textbf&#123;1.5 GHz (16nm)&#125; &amp; 420 kGE \\
\bottomrule
\end&#123;tabular&#125;
\end&#123;table&#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- DETAILED ARCHITECTURAL DOSSIERS FOR CATEGORY 2 CORES -->
  <section class="dossiers-container">
    <div class="section-title-wrap">
      <div class="badge badge-primary">DETAILED ARCHITECTURAL DOSSIERS</div>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Deep-Dive on All Application Cores</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">
        Exhaustive microarchitectural breakdowns, memory buses, MMU translations, silicon evidence, reproduction commands, and complete technical documentation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dossiers-list">
      {cat2Tools.map((tool) => {
        const fallbackContent = tool.slug === "black-parrot" ? blackParrotFallbackReadme : "";
        const rawContent = tool.readmeContent || fallbackContent;
        const renderedMd = rawContent ? renderMarkdown(rawContent) : null;
        return (
          <article class="dossier-card" id={`core-${tool.slug}`}>
            <!-- Dossier Header -->
            <div class="dossier-header">
              <div class="dh-left">
                <span class="d-badge">{tool.language}</span>
                <span class="d-org">{tool.organization}</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dh-right">
                <span class="d-license">{tool.license.split('(')[0]?.trim()}</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="dossier-core-name">{tool.name}</h3>
            <p class="dossier-lead">{tool.subtitle}</p>

            <!-- Specifications Grid -->
            <div class="dossier-specs-grid">
              <div class="ds-col">
                <table class="ds-table">
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><th>Target ISA:</th><td><code>{tool.isa}</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Bus Protocol:</th><td>{tool.bus}</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>HDL Language:</th><td>{tool.language}</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Verification Rigor:</th><td>{tool.verificationEvidence}</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="ds-col">
                <table class="ds-table">
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><th>Silicon Evidence:</th><td>{tool.siliconEvidence}</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>FPGA Readiness:</th><td>{tool.fpgaEvidence}</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Repository Path:</th><td><code>tools/{tool.slug}/</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Files on Disk:</th><td>{tool.fileCount > 0 ? `${tool.fileCount} source files` : "Packaged environment"}</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Architectural Assessment -->
            <div class="dossier-assessment-grid">
              <div class="assess-item strength">
                <strong>&#10003; Strengths:</strong> {tool.notableStrengths}
              </div>
              <div class="assess-item limitation">
                <strong>&#9888; Trade-offs:</strong> {tool.notableLimitations}
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Reproduction Scripts -->
            <div class="dossier-repro-box">
              <span class="repro-title">Reproduction &amp; Verification Commands:</span>
              <div class="repro-cmd-row">
                {tool.scripts.run && (
                  <div class="cmd-item">
                    <span class="cmd-tag">Run Simulation:</span>
                    <code>./{tool.scripts.run}</code>
                  </div>
                )}
                {tool.scripts.generate && (
                  <div class="cmd-item">
                    <span class="cmd-tag">Generate RTL:</span>
                    <code>./{tool.scripts.generate}</code>
                  </div>
                )}
                {tool.scripts.install && (
                  <div class="cmd-item">
                    <span class="cmd-tag">Install Setup:</span>
                    <code>./{tool.scripts.install}</code>
                  </div>
                )}
                {tool.scripts.env && (
                  <div class="cmd-item">
                    <span class="cmd-tag">Environment:</span>
                    <code>source ./{tool.scripts.env}</code>
                  </div>
                )}
                {!tool.scripts.run && !tool.scripts.generate && !tool.scripts.install && (
                  <div class="cmd-item">
                    <span class="cmd-tag">Harness:</span>
                    <code>./scripts/benchmark_core_suite.sh --target={tool.slug}</code>
                  </div>
                )}
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Key Directory Files -->
            {tool.topFiles.length > 0 && (
              <div class="dossier-files-summary">
                <strong>Key Files in <code>tools/{tool.slug}/</code>:</strong>
                <div class="file-tags-wrap">
                  {tool.topFiles.slice(0, 10).map((f) => (
                    <span class="file-tag">{f}</span>
                  ))}
                  {tool.topFiles.length > 10 && (
                    <span class="file-more">+{tool.topFiles.length - 10} more</span>
                  )}
                </div>
              </div>
            )}

            <!-- Interactive README Reader -->
            {renderedMd && (
              <details class="dossier-details-block">
                <summary class="details-summary-btn">
                  &#128196; View Technical Documentation / README ({tool.slug})
                </summary>
                <div class="details-readme-body">
                  <Fragment set:html={renderedMd} />
                </div>
              </details>
            )}
          </article>
        );
      })}

      <!-- BOOM Out-of-Order Reference Core Dossier -->
      <article class="dossier-card" id="core-boom">
        <div class="dossier-header">
          <div class="dh-left">
            <span class="d-badge">Chisel (Scala)</span>
            <span class="d-org">UC Berkeley ADEPT Lab</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dh-right">
            <span class="d-license">BSD-3-Clause</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="dossier-core-name">BOOM (Berkeley Out-of-Order Machine)</h3>
        <p class="dossier-lead">7-to-10 Stage Parameterized Superscalar Out-of-Order Application Processor</p>

        <div class="dossier-specs-grid">
          <div class="ds-col">
            <table class="ds-table">
              <tbody>
                <tr><th>Target ISA:</th><td><code>RV64GC (Sv39/Sv48 MMU)</code></td></tr>
                <tr><th>Bus Protocol:</th><td>TileLink-C (TL-C Coherent)</td></tr>
                <tr><th>HDL Language:</th><td>Chisel v3+ (generates SystemVerilog)</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Verification Rigor:</th><td>RISC-V Torture, riscv-tests, Linux SMP regression</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-col">
            <table class="ds-table">
              <tbody>
                <tr><th>Silicon Evidence:</th><td>Multiple TSMC 16nm / 28nm testchip tapeouts</td></tr>
                <tr><th>FPGA Readiness:</th><td>FireSim cycle-exact AWS EC2 F1 FPGA acceleration</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Repository Path:</th><td>Integrated via Chipyard generator flow</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Pipeline Model:</th><td>1-4 wide decode, 128-entry ROB, PRF renaming</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="dossier-assessment-grid">
          <div class="assess-item strength">
            <strong>&#10003; Strengths:</strong> Highest IPC and memory bandwidth in open-source RISC-V; state-of-the-art TAGE-SC branch prediction; out-of-order memory disambiguation.
          </div>
          <div class="assess-item limitation">
            <strong>&#9888; Trade-offs:</strong> 3&times; area and power overhead compared to in-order cores (~420 kGE); long compile times with Chisel/FIRRTL synthesis.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="dossier-repro-box">
          <span class="repro-title">Reproduction &amp; Verification Commands:</span>
          <div class="repro-cmd-row">
            <div class="cmd-item">
              <span class="cmd-tag">Generate BOOM:</span>
              <code>./scripts/generate_rocket_chip.sh --config=MediumBoomConfig</code>
            </div>
            <div class="cmd-item">
              <span class="cmd-tag">Run Simulation:</span>
              <code>./scripts/run_rocket_chip.sh --binary=bbl_linux.bin</code>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <details class="dossier-details-block">
          <summary class="details-summary-btn">
            &#128196; View Technical Documentation / Architecture Reference (BOOM)
          </summary>
          <div class="details-readme-body">
            <Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(boomFallbackReadme)} />
          </div>
        </details>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Copy LaTeX
  document.querySelectorAll(".copy-latex-btn").forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const targetId = btn.getAttribute("data-target");
      const box = document.getElementById(targetId || "");
      if (box) {
        const isShown = box.style.display === "block";
        box.style.display = isShown ? "none" : "block";
        if (!isShown) {
          const code = box.querySelector("code")?.textContent || "";
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(code).then(() => {
            const orig = btn.textContent;
            btn.textContent = "Copied to Clipboard!";
            setTimeout(() => { btn.textContent = orig; }, 2000);
          });
        }
      }
    });
  });

  document.querySelectorAll(".close-latex-btn").forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
      const parent = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest(".latex-export-box") as HTMLElement;
      if (parent) parent.style.display = "none";
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: var(--cream, #fffaf0);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink, #151b20);
    border-radius: 14px;
    box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px var(--cyan, #22bfd7);
    padding: 2.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .page-header.accent-teal { background: var(--cream, #fffaf0); }

  .page-title {
    font-size: 2.3rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .page-lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink-light);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .core-jump-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed #cccccc;
  }

  .jump-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #333333;
    margin-right: 0.25rem;
  }

  .core-jump-pill {
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 999px;
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.1s ease;
  }

  .core-jump-pill:hover {
    background: var(--cyan);
    transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
    box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--ink);
  }

  .content-block {
    background: var(--cream, #fffaf0);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink, #151b20);
    border-radius: 14px;
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0px var(--ink, #151b20);
    padding: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .block-title {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .block-lead {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--ink-light);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .block-desc {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink-light);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .block-header-flex {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .arch-features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .feature-card {
    background: var(--paper, #f6f0dc);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink, #151b20);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .f-badge {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    background: var(--cyan);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
    width: fit-content;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-light);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .data-table th, .data-table td {
    padding: 0.75rem 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink, #151b20);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .data-table th {
    background: var(--ink, #151b20);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .data-table tr:nth-child(even) td {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.03);
  }

  .score-badge {
    background: var(--cyan);
